{"name":"Sockeye","hex":"#e49780","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sockeye","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small salmon with red flesh, Oncorhynchus nerka, found in the coastal waters of the northern Pacific.","Edible flesh of this fish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sockeye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sockeye salmon","blocks":[{"text":"The sockeye salmon, also called red salmon, kokanee salmon, blueback salmon, or simply sockeye, is an anadromous species of salmon found in the Northern Pacific Ocean and rivers discharging into it. This species is a Pacific salmon that is primarily red in hue during spawning. They can grow up to 84 cm in length and weigh 2.3 to 7 kg (5–15 lb). Juveniles remain in freshwater until they are ready to migrate to the ocean, over distances of up to 1,600 km (1,000 mi). Their diet consists primarily of zooplankton. Sockeye salmon are semelparous, dying after they spawn. Some populations, referred to as kokanee, do not migrate to the ocean and live their entire lives in fresh water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Sockeye_salmon_swimming_right.jpg/330px-Sockeye_salmon_swimming_right.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sockeye_salmon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg/500px-Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg/1280px-Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg/500px-Oncorhynchus_nerka.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male spawning-phase sockeye","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOncorhynchus_nerka.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sockeye_salmon_facing_left.jpg/500px-Sockeye_salmon_facing_left.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sockeye_salmon_facing_left.jpg/500px-Sockeye_salmon_facing_left.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male sockeye salmon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASockeye_salmon_facing_left.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG/500px-SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG/1280px-SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG/500px-SockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spawning sockeye salmon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASockeyeSpawn_inAdams.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg/500px-Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg/1280px-Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg/500px-Red_salmon_or_sockeye_salmon_in_spawning_bed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spawning bed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.